**Concept:**

The equivalent resistance when 'n' resistances are connected in series:

\(R_{eq}=R_1+R_2......R_n\)

The equivalent resistance when 'n' resistances are connected in parallel:

\({1\over R_{eq}}={1\over R_{1}}+{1\over R_{2}}.........{1\over R_{n}}\)

**Calculation:**

Given, R1 = 30 &Omega; 

R2 = 20 &Omega; 

R3 = 60 &Omega; 

\({1\over R_{eq}}={1\over 30}+{1\over 20}+{1\over 60}\)

Req = 10 &Omega;

